))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1456752-i20251211-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-305-a-6","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1456752-i20251211","date":"2025-12-11","original_code":"746.305(a)(6)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-03-09","finding":"Report Situation Placing Children at Risk: The operation failed to notify Child Care Regulation of a serious incident that placed a child at risk.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026607249","violation_type_title":"Report Situation Placing Children at Risk (26 TAC §746.305(a)(6))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1456752-i20251211-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1003-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1456752-i20251211","date":"2025-12-11","original_code":"746.1003(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-03-09","finding":"Director Responsibilities - Operate in Compliance: Due to the numerous deficiencies cited, the former director did not ensure the operation was operating in compliance with the minimum standards.  The former director?s failure to adhere to safety protocols during transitions, and their failure to enforce these protocols amongst staff, directly resulted in a child being left unsupervised.  The former director knowingly provided false information and withheld pertinent details regarding an incident that placed a child at risk.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026607254","violation_type_title":"Director Responsibilities - Operate in Compliance (26 TAC §746.1003(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1456752-i20251211-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-307-b-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1456752-i20251211","date":"2025-12-11","original_code":"746.307(b)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-03-09","finding":"Parental Communication - Situation that Placed a Child at Risk: Based on information obtained during a DFPS investigation, it was determined that the child's parent was not notified of an incident that placed their child at risk of harm.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026607252","violation_type_title":"Parental Communication - Situation that Placed a Child at Risk (26 TAC §746.307(b)(4))","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1456752-i20251211-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-701-5","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1456752-i20251211","date":"2025-12-11","original_code":"746.701(5)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-03-09","finding":"Licensing Incident/Illness Report Form - Situations Placing Children at Risk: Based on information obtained during a DFPS investigation, it was found that an incident report was not completed and shared with the parent when their child was placed at risk.","topic":"health","source_record_id":"1026607251","violation_type_title":"Licensing Incident/Illness Report Form - Situations Placing Children at Risk (26 TAC §746.701(5))","topic_label":"Health records & medication"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1456752-i20251211-v6","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1456752-i20251211","date":"2025-12-11","original_code":"746.1201(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-03-09","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: Based on information obtained during a DFPS investigation, it was determined that a caregiver did not demonstrate good judgement and competency when neglecting to perform the required name-to-face check when transitioning.  This resulted in a child being left unsupervised on the playground.  The caregiver was no aware that the child was not with the group.","topic":"supervision","source_r